found, where , is a sufficiently large prime, and is a character of degree greater than 4.\n\n\n## Citations (5)\n\n## References (14)\n\n... It seems that Hildebrand [14] was the first to study such problems and derive a partial analogue of Halász's theorem for the subsequence of shifted primes. Later, these results have been improved by Timofeev [25] and Khripunova [15]. \nArticle\n\n  * Jan 1968\n\n  * Imre Kátai\n\nView\n\nOn number with small prime divisors\n\nArticle\n\n  * Jan 1956\n  * Dokl Akad Nauk SSSR\n\n  * A.I. Vinogradov\n\nView\n\nÜber die Mittelwerte multiplikativer zahlentheoretischer Funktionen\n\nArticle\n\n  * Sep 1968\n  * ACTA MATH HUNG\n\n  * G. Halász\n\nView\n\nDistribution of values of additive functions on the sequence {p+1}\n\nArticle\n\n  * Jun 1983\n  * MATH NOTES+\n\n  * N. M. Timofeev\n\nView\n\nUniform Distribution of Sequences\n\nArticle\n\n  * Jan 2006\n\n  * Lauwerens Kuipers\n  * H. Niederreiter\n\nView\n\nAdditive and Multiplicative Functions on Shifted Primes\n\nArticle\n\n  * Sep 1989\n\n  * Adolf Hildebrand\n\nWe prove several results on the behaviour of additive and multiplicative arithmetic functions on the sequence {p + 1} of shifted primes. In particular, we establish a complete analogue of the Erdös-Wintner theorem for additive functions, and a partial analogue of Halász's mean value theorem for multiplicative functions. We also give a quantitative mean value estimate for multiplicative functions on shifted primes, and an application to character sums over shifted primes.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Bounded-box reductions in the Subbarao-Warren problem for unitary perfect numbers (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/405089200_Bounded-box_reductions_in_the_Subbarao-Warren_problem_for_unitary_perfect_numbers)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: last month; object is a divisor-randomness or transference-type theorem inspired